====================================================================================================
PART 2 - THE SEPARATING BAND.  Need   retail's cost of waiting  <  premium  <  arb edge.
====================================================================================================
  Fitted: arb edge = 0.581 * sigma_block, essentially independent of the LP fee.
  Retail cost      = lam * sigma_block * sqrt(E[T]),  E[T] = (N+1)/2.
  => sigma CANCELS. Separation exists iff  lam*sqrt((N+1)/2) < 0.581,
     i.e.  N_max = 2*(0.581/lam)^2 - 1.   THE BOUNDARY IS RISK AVERSION, NOT VOLATILITY.

    lam=0.05 -> N_max =    269.5 blocks  (  3234.0s on 12s blocks,    53.9s on Unichain 200ms)   comfortable
    lam=0.10 -> N_max =     66.6 blocks  (   799.5s on 12s blocks,    13.3s on Unichain 200ms)   comfortable
    lam=0.15 -> N_max =     29.1 blocks  (   348.7s on 12s blocks,     5.8s on Unichain 200ms)   comfortable
    lam=0.25 -> N_max =      9.8 blocks  (   117.8s on 12s blocks,     2.0s on Unichain 200ms)   tight
    lam=0.35 -> N_max =      4.5 blocks  (    54.2s on 12s blocks,     0.9s on Unichain 200ms)   DEAD
    lam=0.50 -> N_max =      1.7 blocks  (    20.5s on 12s blocks,     0.3s on Unichain 200ms)   DEAD

  PART 2b - mean-variance alternative, for completeness:
    calm      ~40% ann gam=  1: N_max =          4,694 blocks  -> variance aversion is second-order in sigma at block scale and never binds
    calm      ~40% ann gam=  5: N_max =            939 blocks  -> variance aversion is second-order in sigma at block scale and never binds
    calm      ~40% ann gam= 50: N_max =             94 blocks  -> variance aversion is second-order in sigma at block scale and never binds

====================================================================================================
PART 3 - is an IRREVOCABLE, no-minOut deferred order an OPTION or a FORWARD?
====================================================================================================
  calm      ~40% ann N=  10  E[P_T]-P_0 =  -0.0008 bps   sd =     5.79 bps
  calm      ~40% ann N=  50  E[P_T]-P_0 =  -0.0032 bps   sd =    12.48 bps
  calm      ~40% ann N= 300  E[P_T]-P_0 =  +0.1101 bps   sd =    30.30 bps
  normal    ~60% ann N=  10  E[P_T]-P_0 =  +0.0047 bps   sd =     8.65 bps
  normal    ~60% ann N=  50  E[P_T]-P_0 =  -0.0424 bps   sd =    18.66 bps
  normal    ~60% ann N= 300  E[P_T]-P_0 =  -0.0416 bps   sd =    45.41 bps
  stressed ~120% ann N=  10  E[P_T]-P_0 =  +0.0104 bps   sd =    17.37 bps
  stressed ~120% ann N=  50  E[P_T]-P_0 =  +0.0895 bps   sd =    37.42 bps
  stressed ~120% ann N= 300  E[P_T]-P_0 =  -0.1278 bps   sd =    90.64 bps
  longtail ~300% ann N=  10  E[P_T]-P_0 =  -0.0202 bps   sd =    43.44 bps
  longtail ~300% ann N=  50  E[P_T]-P_0 =  -0.0550 bps   sd =    93.55 bps
  longtail ~300% ann N= 300  E[P_T]-P_0 =  +0.0833 bps   sd =   227.11 bps
  => payoff is LINEAR in P_T. Zero expected gain, zero gamma. It is a forward with
     random delivery, NOT an option. A delta-neutral placer harvests nothing.

====================================================================================================
PART 4 - value of a FREE minOut refund. THIS is the actual option.
  Value above an unconditional fill = E[(K - P_T)+], a free PUT struck at the tolerance.
  The ONLY thing that matters is z = tol / (sigma_b * sqrt(E[T])) - how many standard
  deviations out of the money the refund trigger sits. Value below is in units of the
  interim move sigma_b*sqrt(E[T]), so one table covers every vol regime.
====================================================================================================
 z (tol in sd)  put/sd MC closed form    @N=10    @N=50  refund rate   verdict
          0.00     0.3984      0.3989    1.61x    3.46x        49.9%   FATAL - free option dwarfs the premium
          0.25     0.2856      0.2863    1.15x    2.48x        40.1%   FATAL - free option dwarfs the premium
          0.50     0.1976      0.1978    0.80x    1.72x        30.9%   DANGEROUS
          1.00     0.0835      0.0833    0.34x    0.72x        15.9%   DANGEROUS
          1.50     0.0291      0.0293    0.12x    0.25x         6.6%   safe - refund is deep OTM
          2.00     0.0085      0.0085    0.03x    0.07x         2.3%   safe - refund is deep OTM
          3.00     0.0004      0.0004    0.00x    0.00x         0.1%   safe - refund is deep OTM
          4.00     0.0000      0.0000    0.00x    0.00x         0.0%   safe - refund is deep OTM

  => DESIGN RULE, and it is enforceable on-chain because the hook already measures
     sigma_b for the premium: REJECT any deferred order whose minOut sits closer than
     ~2 sd of the interim move. At z>=2 the free put is worth <7% of the arb edge and
     the refund fires <3% of the time. At z=0 (fill-only-if-improved) it is worth more
     than the entire arb edge and HASTE is a straddle written by the LPs.

====================================================================================================
PART 4b - does the premium actually help LPs, or does it just buy price staleness?
  LP net vs ARB FLOW ONLY = fee+premium revenue - LVR. Retail revenue is excluded
  because retail's response to the premium is the thing under test elsewhere.
====================================================================================================
regime               total friction  arb rev/blk   LVR/blk  LP net/blk  staleness
normal    ~60% ann               5b       0.0240    0.0165      0.0075      3.34b
normal    ~60% ann              10b       0.0284    0.0122      0.0162      5.95b
normal    ~60% ann              20b       0.0312    0.0092      0.0220     11.06b
normal    ~60% ann              50b       0.0330    0.0073      0.0257     25.98b
normal    ~60% ann             100b       0.0346    0.0048      0.0298     51.34b
stressed ~120% ann               5b       0.0740    0.0900     -0.0161      3.88b
stressed ~120% ann              10b       0.0964    0.0676      0.0288      6.69b
stressed ~120% ann              20b       0.1137    0.0502      0.0635     11.90b
stressed ~120% ann              50b       0.1274    0.0361      0.0913     27.22b
stressed ~120% ann             100b       0.1320    0.0306      0.1013     52.08b
  => staleness tracks the friction almost 1:1. The premium is NOT paid out of the
     arb's per-notional edge (which is fee-invariant, Part 1); it is paid by widening
     the no-arb band. LPs still gain, because LVR falls faster than arb revenue, but
     the immediate lane's true cost to an urgent trader is premium + staleness ~ 2x premium.

